# Helios agent integration — environment template
#
# Copy to .env, fill in, then load it:
#     cp .env.example .env
#     set -a; source .env; set +a          # bash / zsh
# Then check the connection before running an agent:
#     agent-integration doctor
#
# .env is gitignored; .env.example is not. Nothing here is required: with no
# token at all, `demo`, `selfcheck`, `inspect` and `run --offline` all work,
# and grants are signed with an ephemeral process key.

# --- Model (the action agent) ---------------------------------------------
#
# GLM-5.3 over the OpenAI-compatible Chat Completion protocol. The token is
# sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` — plain, not the legacy JWT shape,
# which GLM-5.3 rejects.
#
# Accepted variable names, in priority order:
#   HELIOS_LLM_API_KEY, LLM_API_TOKEN, GLM_API_KEY, ZHIPUAI_API_KEY
HELIOS_LLM_API_KEY=

# Model id. glm-5.3 is the flagship; glm-5.3-flash is cheaper and faster.
# GLM-5.3 always reasons — there is no way to turn thinking off.
HELIOS_LLM_MODEL=glm-5.3

# Endpoint. Leave this at the public URL UNLESS your token came from a
# gateway. A token shaped like `L2...` rather than `sk-...` usually means it
# was issued by an organisation's own gateway, and that gateway has its own
# base URL — the public one will reject the token with a 401.
#
# Public GLM endpoints:
#   https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4    (mainland China)
#   https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4            (international)
#
# Override with `--base-url` on the command line if you prefer.
HELIOS_LLM_BASE_URL=https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4

# Reasoning depth: low | high | max. `max` is the model default and the most
# expensive. `high` is a reasonable middle ground for tool use; `low` is used
# automatically by `doctor`.
HELIOS_LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=high

# Output cap per turn. GLM-5.3 allows up to 131072, but an agent turn is a
# tool call or a short sentence, so 4096 is plenty and much cheaper.
HELIOS_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=4096

# --- Audit signing ---------------------------------------------------------
# The audit agent signs every grant with HMAC-SHA256. Without this key it
# falls back to an ephemeral process key: the replay and tamper checks still
# run, but grants do not survive a restart and two processes cannot verify
# each other. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
HELIOS_AUDIT_SIGNING_KEY=

# A label recorded on grants so you can tell which key signed what. This is
# never the key itself.
HELIOS_AUDIT_SIGNING_KEY_ID=helios-audit-local

# --- Runtime shape ---------------------------------------------------------
# How the action agent reaches the auditor: inprocess | file | http
# `http` is the deployment shape — the auditor as its own service, reachable
# only through the contract, never by import.
HELIOS_AUDIT_TRANSPORT=inprocess

# Where run state and audit evidence are written.
HELIOS_RUNS_DIR=.runs
HELIOS_DATA_DIR=.helios-data
